0..78 Comment "// An atom named inside the abstraction that binds it, read by its depth below"
79..93 Comment "// its binder."
94..96 Comment "//"
97..172 Comment "// Admission re-mints an atom with its binder, so a rule naming the channel"
173..249 Comment "// its restriction abstracts is one rule whatever the atom is called. A rule"
250..326 Comment "// stating a freshness condition fires only where its instance names no atom"
327..341 Comment "// it may not."
342..344 Comment "//"
345..423 Comment "// Matching, the critical pairs and the kernel\'s replay count the abstractions"
424..501 Comment "// between an occurrence and its binder. A rule\'s variable is a hole over the"
502..578 Comment "// atoms it may name, so the check decides an overlap under the condition it"
579..648 Comment "// composes. Each theory below normalizes one process its rules meet."
649..651 Comment "//"
652..713 Comment "// - owes: #1934 — a rule matching a variable both under an"
714..744 Comment "//   abstraction and beside it"
745..819 Comment "// - see: `pathological/desc/atom-occurrence.gandr` — that rule, refused"
820..888 Comment "// - see: Fernández and Gabbay, _Nominal rewriting_, I&C 2007, § 2"
889..936 Comment "// - see: Pitts, _Nominal Sets_, CUP 2013, § 4"
937..1016 Comment "// - see: Milner, _Communicating and Mobile Systems: the π-Calculus_, CUP 1999"
1017..1083 Comment "// - see: Mayr and Nipkow, _Higher-order rewrite systems and their"
1084..1110 Comment "//   confluence_, TCS 1998"
1111..1183 Comment "// - see: Miller, _A logic programming language with lambda-abstraction,"
1184..1242 Comment "//   function variables, and simple unification_, JLC 1991"
1244..1320 Comment "/// A send on a restricted channel, which no process outside the restriction"
1321..1398 Comment "/// can receive: the process never moves, so it is the inert one. The checker"
1399..1475 Comment "/// orients the law and the kernel replays the verdict; a restriction naming"
1476..1535 Comment "/// its channel `b` normalizes by the law written over `a`."
1536..1538 Other "@["
1539..1549 Other "normalizes"
1549..1550 Other "("
1550..1551 StringLit "\""
1551..1582 StringLit "nu(bind b . out(b, nil)) ~> nil"
1582..1583 StringLit "\""
1583..1584 Other ")"
1585..1586 Other "]"
